{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/261534-armor-rules","id":261534,"title":"Armor rules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-20T15:24:01-07:00","id":261534,"title":"Armor rules","content":"So what does armor do to an attack roll in OWoD? Does the Dex penalty subtract from Firearms rolls? What about Brawl or Melee? The rules are pretty undefined on these things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Armor adds its rating to the character\u2019s soak<br /> dice pool against bashing damage, lethal<br /> damage, and aggravated damage from fangs<br /> and claws. It does not protect against fire<br /> or sunlight. However, armor also subtracts<br /> a number of dice from dice pools related to<br /> bodily coordination and agility (most Dexter-<br /> ity-based dice pools). This is reflected in the<br /> penalty listing. Attackers may make targeting<br /> rolls to hit unprotected portions of a defender<br /> and thus ignore the armor (Storyteller assigns<br /> difficulty penalty \u2014 typically +1 or +2). </div> </div> </div>And I can't seem to find a clarification any where for it. Anyone have any ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T17:11:44-07:00","id":261603,"title":"","content":"Armor is, generally speaking, designed with fighting in mind. Impeding attacks is pretty much against the point. Trying to do gymnastics, or do fine metal work on jewelry while wearing metal gauntlets is not so easy.<br /> <br /> The rules don't really clarify though and leave it up to the ST. Sorry that there's no real help besides, &quot;what feels right.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T20:59:27-07:00","id":262637,"title":"","content":"Thankfully, we have no concept of armor class in wod. Armor does absolutely nothing on the attack roll besides, perhaps, making it harder to dodge (as stated by the dex pool reference). I do not see what is unclear about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3870-tritium","name":"Tritium","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T17:33:21-07:00","id":263274,"title":"","content":"Yeah, dodge seems like it's covered by the penalty. Athletics-type stuff probably too, even if you'd normally use a strength roll for it, so good luck climbing or jumping rooftops or whatever. Guns are absolutely not agility based, so no penalty there...combining agility and dexterity into one attribute is a longstanding sin of RPGs. A particularly mean GM might say that the armor penalty applies to some H2H stuff, but I'd mostly disagree...mostly. Fencing, as agility based as it is, probably wouldn't be hurt by armor: your stance is one where it wouldn't get in the way. Boxing also takes a lot of agility, but I wouldn't really give armor penalties, because you can worry less about taking a hit and adjust your style to fit. But Aikido? yeah, you want to do aikido in plate mail, you're taking some penalties, there's a lot of rolling on the ground and whirling around behind people. Maybe assign penalties on a move by move basis, dunno. Likewise you'd surely take penalties to Expression:Breakdancing...but if you just take off your heavy gauntlets and leave the rest intact, no penalty on Expression:Painting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}